  "An Ochorus Original whose English quotes the King James Version; every quotation in this French edition is Louis Segond 1910, pasted byte-for-byte by script (epigraph references in capitals, Segond numbering, e.g. PSAUME 46:11, PSAUME 80:15, 1 PIERRE 2:7–8). Where the English argues from a KJV wording Segond lacks, the KJV reading is rendered into French and Segond's own words are given beside it: Galates 5:22 « la foi » (Segond « la fidélité »), Galates 2:20 « la foi du Fils de Dieu » (Segond « la foi au Fils de Dieu »), Ésaïe 40:31 « attendre » (Segond « se confient »). The about text and attribution say that the English quotes the King James Version and this edition quotes Segond. Rows come from two passes: every printed reference (mined where the block carries a verbatim Segond span of 45+ characters), and every quoted French span of 30+ characters that occurs verbatim in exactly one Segond verse.",
